WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.982
On this slide, we are focusing on reusable calculator function.

00:00:03.982 --> 00:00:09.077
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:09.077 --> 00:00:15.312
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:18.942
A function gives a reusable task a clear name.

00:00:18.942 --> 00:00:26.787
In analytics, functions are useful for cleaning, validation, scoring, calculation, and reporting logic.

00:00:26.787 --> 00:00:29.972
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:29.972 --> 00:00:36.117
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:36.117 --> 00:00:39.462
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:44.474
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
